<blockquote>
<p>“A standard steel-reinforced 3 x 3 x 1 x 1 meter 4-doorway is to be hyperspatially installed around SCP-4357”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm trying to indicate that this is a 4-dimensional portal, isolating it from parallel realities as explained later.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Use meters instead of feet.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you're referring to the American 6'8&quot; doorway, that's a standardized size for doorframes in the American construction industry. Saying a &quot;2.032 meter door&quot; wouldn't make sense, when the common term is &quot;6-8 door.&quot; The Foundation constructs and measures everything in metric, but most of America doesn't, so using standard industry terms sometimes means using Imperial.</p>
<p>Another example of this would be if the Foundation comes across something that had been built with 1/4 inch screws. It wouldn't make sense to say &quot;6.35 millimeter screws,&quot; because the item that is called a &quot;1/4 inch screw&quot; refers to a specific, standardized product with a particular thread count. There's no such thing as a &quot;6.35 millimeter screw.&quot;</p>

							</div>

								
